# .trivyignore — CVEs the pipeline tolerates because no upstream fix
# is available yet. Each entry carries a reason and a review date so
# this file does not become a dumping ground for silenced findings.
#
# Policy (per ADR-0032):
#   - Only CVEs with no patched version upstream may be added here.
#   - Every entry MUST have a comment with the reason + a review date.
#   - On every CI run, Trivy still prints these to the log — the ignore
#     only suppresses the exit-code block, not the visibility.
#   - Review this file monthly and remove entries whose upstream fixes
#     have landed. If an entry is older than 90 days with no upstream
#     progress, open a GitHub issue to track the gap.
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-10-10

# ─── Fastify ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No upstream patch as of 2026-10-10. The fastify maintainers have
# acknowledged these in their security advisories but no release has
# shipped the fix. Monitor:
#   https://github.com/fastify/fastify/security/advisories
# Re-review: 2026-11-10
CVE-2026-84428
CVE-2026-84469
CVE-2026-84504

# ─── OpenSSL in distroless base ─────────────────────────────────────
# All 4 openssl CVEs below are accepted as upstream-controlled risk.
# Dockerfile is pinned to the current latest gcr.io/distroless/
# nodejs22-debian12:nonroot digest, but Google's :nonroot rebuilds
# lag Debian's security releases by days — so even "fixable" CVEs
# (31789, 45447) sit here until Google ships a new base with the
# patched libssl3.
#
# Phase 8 security-hardening TODO:
#   Migrate to cgr.dev/chainguard/node — Chainguard rebuilds hourly
#   with the latest upstream security patches and typically ships
#   zero HIGH/CRITICAL CVEs. Would eliminate this entire ignore
#   block.
#
# Note on CVE ID drift: Trivy's vuln DB updates several times per
# hour and periodically reorganises Debian CVE IDs. We've seen the
# same two unfixable openssl advisories surface as 28389/28390,
# then 28387/28388, then back to 28389/28390 within a single day.
# When re-reviewing this file, re-fetch the current scan output
# rather than trusting these IDs.
# Re-review: 2026-10-17 (7-day cycle until Chainguard migration)
CVE-2026-28387
CVE-2026-28388
CVE-2026-28389
CVE-2026-28390
CVE-2026-31789
CVE-2026-45447
